              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="alg2.l27.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> each </span><math id="alg2.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in\mathcal{T}_{\text{sel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">sel</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in\mathcal{T}_{\text{sel}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l27.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg2.l27.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">do</span><span id="alg2.l27.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l28.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  Compute color </span><math id="alg2.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{i}\leftarrow\text{ColorMap}(t_{i}/K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐜</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">ColorMap</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{i}\leftarrow\text{ColorMap}(t_{i}/K)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l28.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l29.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  Overlay index and color on </span><math id="alg2.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t_{i}}\Rightarrow\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℱ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t_{i}}\Rightarrow\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l29.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg2.l30.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg2.l30.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Trajectory Visualization:</span><span id="alg2.l31.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg2.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\text{BEV}}\leftarrow\text{ProjectXY}(\mathcal{T}^{\text{world}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐏</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">BEV</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">ProjectXY</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">world</mtext></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\text{BEV}}\leftarrow\text{ProjectXY}(\mathcal{T}^{\text{world}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l31.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="alg2.l31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\text{3D}}\leftarrow\text{Render3D}(\mathcal{T}^{\text{world}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐏</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">3D</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Render3D</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">world</mtext></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\text{3D}}\leftarrow\text{Render3D}(\mathcal{T}^{\text{world}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l31.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Motion Reconstruction</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we recall the mathematical context of Visual Odometry (VO). <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that most of these can be found in the textbooks.</span> The first step of VO is need to conduct ORB (Oriented FAST and Rotated BRIEF) Feature Detection and Description, then Feature Matching, finally perform Essential Matrix Estimation. For this part of algorithm development, we leverage OpenCV <span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python</a></span></span></span> for efficient deployment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ORB Feature Detection and Description.</span> In detailed, ORB combines FAST keypoint detection with orientation-augmented BRIEF descriptors, producing a scale- and rotation-invariant feature. Regarding <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Keypoint Detection (FAST)</span>: Given a grayscale image <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}:\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}:\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the FAST corner detector selects a pixel <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> as a keypoint if there exists a contiguous arc of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> pixels on the Bresenham circle <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\mathbf{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\mathbf{p})</annotation></semantics></math> of radius 3 around <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that:</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{t}(\mathbf{q})-f_{t}(\mathbf{p})|&gt;\tau,\hskip 10.00002pt\forall\mathbf{q}\in C_{n}(\mathbf{p})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{t}(\mathbf{q})-f_{t}(\mathbf{p})|&gt;\tau,\hskip 10.00002pt\forall\mathbf{q}\in C_{n}(\mathbf{p}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}(\mathbf{p})\subset C(\mathbf{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}(\mathbf{p})\subset C(\mathbf{p})</annotation></semantics></math> is a contiguous segment of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> pixels, and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is a contrast threshold. Typically, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=12</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C(\mathbf{p})|=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C(\mathbf{p})|=16</annotation></semantics></math>. This step yields the raw keypoint set <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{t}=\left\{\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}\in\Omega\right\}_{i=1}^{N}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{t}=\left\{\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}\in\Omega\right\}_{i=1}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of detected corners in frame <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Regarding <span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Orientation Assignment</span>, to achieve rotation invariance, ORB computes the orientation angle <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of each keypoint <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by using intensity moments of a patch <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> around the keypoint:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}=\arctan\left(\frac{m_{01}}{m_{10}}\right),\hskip 10.00002ptm_{pq}=\sum_{\mathbf{q}\in P_{i}}x^{p}y^{q}f_{t}(\mathbf{q})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arctan</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}=\arctan\left(\frac{m_{01}}{m_{10}}\right),\hskip 10.00002ptm_{pq}=\sum_{\mathbf{q}\in P_{i}}x^{p}y^{q}f_{t}(\mathbf{q}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> are coordinates relative to the keypoint <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we perform <span id="A1.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Descriptor Computation (BRIEF)</span>. The BRIEF descriptor <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{t}\in{0,1}^{N\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{t}\in{0,1}^{N\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed by binary intensity comparisons between <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D/2</annotation></semantics></math> pre-defined point pairs <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{a}_{k},\mathbf{b}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{a}_{k},\mathbf{b}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> in the local patch around each <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, rotated by angle <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{t}(i,k)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\mathrm{if~}f_{t}(R_{\theta_{i}}\mathbf{a}_{k}+\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t})&lt;f_{t}(R_{\theta_{i}}\mathbf{b}_{k}+\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}),\\
0&amp;\mathrm{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>otherwise</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{t}(i,k)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\mathrm{if~}f_{t}(R_{\theta_{i}}\mathbf{a}_{k}+\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t})&lt;f_{t}(R_{\theta_{i}}\mathbf{b}_{k}+\mathbf{p}_{i}^{t}),\\
0&amp;\mathrm{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\theta_{i}}\in SO(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\theta_{i}}\in SO(2)</annotation></semantics></math> is the 2D rotation matrix corresponding to <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feature Matching.</span> Given two sets of ORB descriptors <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{t-1},\mathcal{D}_{t}\in{0,1}^{N\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{t-1},\mathcal{D}_{t}\in{0,1}^{N\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>, feature correspondences are established by computing Hamming distances between binary descriptor vectors. For each descriptor <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d}i^{t-1}\in\mathcal{D}{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐝</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}i^{t-1}\in\mathcal{D}{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the matching descriptor in frame <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d}_{j}^{t}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{d}\in\mathcal{D}_{t}}\mathrm{Hamming}(\mathbf{d}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{d})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝐝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Hamming</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}_{j}^{t}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{d}\in\mathcal{D}_{t}}\mathrm{Hamming}(\mathbf{d}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and accept the match if the distance is below a threshold <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> or passes Lowe’s ratio test. Let the resulting matched keypoint pairs be:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t-1,t}=\left\{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t})\right\}_{i=1}^{P},\hskip 10.00002pt\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t-1,t}=\left\{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t})\right\}_{i=1}^{P},\hskip 10.00002pt\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}i^{t-1}=\mathbf{p}{a_{i}}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}i^{t-1}=\mathbf{p}{a_{i}}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}i^{t}=\mathbf{p}{b_{i}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}i^{t}=\mathbf{p}{b_{i}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to matched keypoints.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Essential Matrix Estimation.</span> Given matched pixel coordinates <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{x}i^{t})}{i=1}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1},\mathbf{x}i^{t})}{i=1}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and the intrinsic matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{3\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{3\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math>, normalized coordinates are computed:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t-1}=\mathbf{K}^{-1}\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1}\\
1\end{bmatrix},\hskip 10.00002pt\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t}=\mathbf{K}^{-1}\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}\\
1\end{bmatrix},\hskip 10.00002pt\hat{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t-1}=\mathbf{K}^{-1}\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t-1}\\
1\end{bmatrix},\hskip 10.00002pt\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t}=\mathbf{K}^{-1}\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}\\
1\end{bmatrix},\hskip 10.00002pt\hat{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The essential matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}\in\mathbb{R}^{3\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}\in\mathbb{R}^{3\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes the relative motion such that <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t})^{\top}\mathbf{E}\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t-1}=0,\forall i." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t})^{\top}\mathbf{E}\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t-1}=0,\forall i.</annotation></semantics></math> In matrix terms, stacking all equations gives:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\cdot\mathrm{vec}(\mathbf{E})=0,\mathrm{where~}\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times 9}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>where</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\cdot\mathrm{vec}(\mathbf{E})=0,\mathrm{where~}\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times 9}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">This is solved via SVD of <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> in the 8-point algorithm, or a robust estimator such as:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{E}^{\prime}}\sum_{i}\rho\left((\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t})^{\top}\mathbf{E^{\prime}}\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t-1}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><msup><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{E}^{\prime}}\sum_{i}\rho\left((\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t})^{\top}\mathbf{E^{\prime}}\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}^{t-1}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a robust loss (e.g., truncated quadratic), and outliers are rejected via RANSAC. Since <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy the singular value constraint <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}=\sigma_{2},\sigma_{3}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}=\sigma_{2},\sigma_{3}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we project it onto the essential matrix manifold via SVD:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}=\mathbf{U}\cdot\mathrm{diag}(1,1,0)\cdot\mathbf{V}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}=\mathbf{U}\cdot\mathrm{diag}(1,1,0)\cdot\mathbf{V}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p">Finally, we decompose the essential matrix to motion. Specially, The essential matrix relates to the relative pose via: <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}=[\mathbf{T}_{t}]_{\times}\mathbf{R}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐓</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>×</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}=[\mathbf{T}_{t}]_{\times}\mathbf{R}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\cdot]_{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>×</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\cdot]_{\times}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the skew-symmetric matrix:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathbf{T}_{t}]_{\times}=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;-T_{z}&amp;T_{y}\\
T_{z}&amp;0&amp;-T_{x}\\
-T_{y}&amp;T_{x}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐓</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>×</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathbf{T}_{t}]_{\times}=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;-T_{z}&amp;T_{y}\\
T_{z}&amp;0&amp;-T_{x}\\
-T_{y}&amp;T_{x}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.6" class="ltx_p">The decomposition of <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}</annotation></semantics></math> via SVD provides four candidate solutions <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pm\mathbf{R}_{t},\pm\mathbf{T}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><msub><mi>𝐓</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pm\mathbf{R}_{t},\pm\mathbf{T}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, disambiguated by the Cheirality condition—checking the number of triangulated points in front of both cameras.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Joint Optimized Prompting</h3>

<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.16087v1/visual-prompt.png" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/190;" width="476" height="190" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>The sample of the visual prompting input in <span id="A1.F4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we give the sample of our general input containing text and vision for <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MLLMs</span> evaluation. For <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Internvl3-8B</span>, after spatial prompting from <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span>, the visual inputs are as shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ A.3 Joint Optimized Prompting ‣ Appendix A Methods ‣ See&amp;Trek: Training-Free Spatial Prompting for Multimodal Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, then we also design the corresponding text prompt template as shown in <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ A.3 Joint Optimized Prompting ‣ Appendix A Methods ‣ See&amp;Trek: Training-Free Spatial Prompting for Multimodal Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. “Points” denotes the relative spatial coordinates of each selected frames. Since different MLLMs have different training data, architectures, and training methods, using text prompts or point coordinates as prompts has a particularly large impact on performance. Therefore, we fine-tune the instructions for different model series to enable <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span> to fully utilize its spatial understanding advantages.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="A1.F5.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_align_center ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;--ltx-border-color:#000000;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">spatial_prompt_universal</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">=</span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">(</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;">"Each<span id="lstnumberx2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>video<span id="lstnumberx2.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>frame<span id="lstnumberx2.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>has<span id="lstnumberx2.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>its<span id="lstnumberx2.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>serial<span id="lstnumberx2.3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>number<span id="lstnumberx2.3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>in<span id="lstnumberx2.3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx2.3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>top-right<span id="lstnumberx2.3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>corner.<span id="lstnumberx2.3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>"</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;">"The<span id="lstnumberx3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>highlight<span id="lstnumberx3.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>color<span id="lstnumberx3.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>mark<span id="lstnumberx3.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>of<span id="lstnumberx3.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>frame<span id="lstnumberx3.3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>matches<span id="lstnumberx3.3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx3.3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>color<span id="lstnumberx3.3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>in<span id="lstnumberx3.3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx3.3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>spatial<span id="lstnumberx3.3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>map,<span id="lstnumberx3.3.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>indicating<span id="lstnumberx3.3.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>its<span id="lstnumberx3.3.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>position."</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">spatial_prompt_2D_3D</span><span id="lstnumberx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">=</span><span id="lstnumberx5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">(</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;">"Both<span id="lstnumberx6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>2D<span id="lstnumberx6.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>(bird’s-eye)<span id="lstnumberx6.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>and<span id="lstnumberx6.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>3D<span id="lstnumberx6.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>views<span id="lstnumberx6.3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>illustrate<span id="lstnumberx6.3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx6.3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>camera’s<span id="lstnumberx6.3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>spatial<span id="lstnumberx6.3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>trajectory,<span id="lstnumberx6.3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>"</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;">"with<span id="lstnumberx7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>color<span id="lstnumberx7.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>encoding<span id="lstnumberx7.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>time<span id="lstnumberx7.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>progression."</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">spatial_prompt_points</span><span id="lstnumberx9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">=</span><span id="lstnumberx9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx9.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">(</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;">"Points<span id="lstnumberx10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>represent<span id="lstnumberx10.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx10.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>camera’s<span id="lstnumberx10.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>relative<span id="lstnumberx10.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>positions;<span id="lstnumberx10.3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx10.3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>number<span id="lstnumberx10.3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>of<span id="lstnumberx10.3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>points<span id="lstnumberx10.3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>reflects<span id="lstnumberx10.3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>only<span id="lstnumberx10.3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>spatial<span id="lstnumberx10.3.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>relationships."</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">input_prompt</span><span id="lstnumberx12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">=</span><span id="lstnumberx12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">spatial_prompt_universal</span><span id="lstnumberx12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">+</span><span id="lstnumberx12.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">spatial_prompt_2D_3D</span><span id="lstnumberx12.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">+</span><span id="lstnumberx12.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">spatial_prompt_points</span><span id="lstnumberx12.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">+</span><span id="lstnumberx12.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">points</span><span id="lstnumberx12.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">+</span><span id="lstnumberx12.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;">"\n"</span><span id="lstnumberx12.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">+</span><span id="lstnumberx12.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">question</span>
</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>The sample of the text prompting input in <span id="A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span>. “Points” denotes the relative spatial coordinates of each selected frames.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>VSI-Bench Dataset</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overview.</span> <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> includes eight tasks of three types: <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">configurational</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">measurement estimation</span>, and <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">spatiotemporal</span>. The configurational tasks (<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">object count</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">relative distance</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">relative direction</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">route plan</span>) test a model’s understanding of the configuration of space and are more intuitive for humans. Measurement estimation (of <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">object size</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">room size</span>, and <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">absolute distance</span>) is of value to any embodied agent. While predicting a measurement exactly is very difficult, for both humans and models, a better sense of distance and other measurements is intuitively correlated with better visual-spatial intelligence and underpins a wide range of tasks that require spatial awareness, like interaction with objects and navigation. Spatiotemporal tasks like appearance order test a model’s memory of space as seen in the video.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric Design.</span> Based on whether the ground-truth answer is verbal or numerical, <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> tasks are suited to either a Multiple-Choice Answer (MCA) or Numerical Answer (NA) format. For MCA tasks, <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> follows standard practice by using <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Accuracy</span> (<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{ACC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{ACC}</annotation></semantics></math>), based on exact matching (with possible fuzzy matching), as the primary metric. For NA tasks, where models predict continuous values, accuracy via exact matching fails to capture the degree of proximity between model predictions and ground-truth answers. Therefore, <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> utilizes a new metric, <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mean Relative Accuracy</span> (<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{MRA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{MRA}</annotation></semantics></math>) inspired by previous works. Specifically, for a NA question, given a model’s prediction <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, ground truth <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and a confidence threshold <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, relative accuracy is calculated by considering <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math> correct if the relative error rate, defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{y}-y|/y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{y}-y|/y</annotation></semantics></math>, is less than <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. As single-confidence-threshold accuracy only considers relative error in a narrow scope, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{MRA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{MRA}</annotation></semantics></math> averages the relative accuracy across a range of confidence thresholds <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{0.5,0.55,...,0.95\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.55</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{0.5,0.55,...,0.95\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{MRA}=\frac{1}{10}\sum_{\theta\in\mathcal{C}}\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{|\hat{y}-y|}{y}&lt;1-\theta\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{MRA}=\frac{1}{10}\sum_{\theta\in\mathcal{C}}\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{|\hat{y}-y|}{y}&lt;1-\theta\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{MRA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{MRA}</annotation></semantics></math> offers a more reliable and discriminative measurement for calculating the similarity between numerical predictions and ground truth values.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Chance Level Baselines</span>. <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> provides two baselines: 1) <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Chance Level</span> (Random) is the random selection accuracy for MCA tasks (and is inapplicable for NA tasks). 2) <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Chance Level</span> (Frequency) represents the highest performance <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MLLMs</span> would achieve by always selecting the most frequent answer for each task. This identifies performance gains that may result from inherently long-tailed answers or imbalanced multiple-choice distributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Human Level Performance.</span> <span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> randomly sample a subset of 400 questions (50 per task), which we will refer to as <span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> (tiny). Human evaluators independently answer each question, and their performance is evaluated using the above-mentioned metrics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.16087v1/results_1.png" id="A2.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/353;" width="476" height="353" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Qualitative results about <span id="A2.F6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span> evaluated on <span id="A2.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span>. Here, we represent the different tasks of (a) Route Plan (b) Object Absolute Size (Obj. Size), and (c) Object Relative Distance (Rel. Dist.).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.16087v1/results_2.png" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/329;" width="476" height="329" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Qualitative results about <span id="A2.F7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span> evaluated on <span id="A2.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span>. Here, we represent the different tasks of (d) Object Count (Obj. Count) (e) Object Absolute Distance (Abs. Dist.), and (f) Appearance Order (Appr. Order).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.16087v1/results_3.png" id="A2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/237;" width="476" height="237" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Qualitative results about <span id="A2.F8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span> evaluated on <span id="A2.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span>. Here, we represent the different tasks of (g) Route Plan (h) Object Relative Direction (Rel. Dir.)</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>STI-Bench Dataset</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overview.</span> <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">STI-Bench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> contains 300 videos and more than 2,000 QA pairs, covering three major scenarios: Desktop, Indoor, and Outdoor. The videos are sourced from <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Omni6DPose</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>, <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ScanNet</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> and <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Waymo</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> respectively, thus encompassing a broad spectrum of real-world environments. They propose eight tasks in total, each one systematically examining a distinct aspect of MLLMs’ spatial-temporal understanding, which divide these tasks into two main categories: 1) <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Static Understanding</span>: <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dimensional Measurement, Spatial Relation, 3D Video Grounding</span>; 2) <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamic Understanding</span>: <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Displacement and Path Length</span>, <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Speed and Acceleration, Ego-Centric Orientation, Trajectory Description</span> and <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Pose Estimation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">API Engine and Baseline Settings.</span> Regarding the commercial engine, <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">STI-Bench</span> uniformly sample 30 frames from the video for each record and explicitly indicate the sampling FPS (Frames Per Second) for the current video within the prompt. An exception is made for Claude3.7-Sonnet, for which only 20 frames are sampled due to its API constraints. <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">STI-Bench</span> are presented in a multiple-choice format with five possible answers, hence a random guess baseline yields a 20% accuracy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric Design.</span> 1) <span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dimensional Measurement.</span> let <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{x},l_{y},l_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{x},l_{y},l_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the dimensions (length, width, height) of an object along the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> axes:</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{x}=x_{\max}-x_{\min},l_{y}=y_{\max}-y_{\min},l_{z}=z_{\max}-z_{\min}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{x}=x_{\max}-x_{\min},l_{y}=y_{\max}-y_{\min},l_{z}=z_{\max}-z_{\min},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{x},l_{y},l_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{x},l_{y},l_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the object size along each coordinate axis. If it needs the distance between two objects (or between the camera and an object), let <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{12}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Euclidean distance between their center points:</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{12}=\sqrt{(x_{2}-x_{1})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{1})^{2}+(z_{2}-z_{1})^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{12}=\sqrt{(x_{2}-x_{1})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{1})^{2}+(z_{2}-z_{1})^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1},z_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1},z_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{2},y_{2},z_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{2},y_{2},z_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> are the center coordinates of the two objects.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">2) <span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Spatial Relation.</span> When the difference along one coordinate axis is significantly larger than along others, the sign of that difference determines the spatial relation:</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{xy}=\mathrm{sign}(x_{A}-x_{B}),r_{yz}=\mathrm{sign}(y_{A}-y_{B}),r_{zx}=\mathrm{sign}(z_{A}-z_{B})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{xy}=\mathrm{sign}(x_{A}-x_{B}),r_{yz}=\mathrm{sign}(y_{A}-y_{B}),r_{zx}=\mathrm{sign}(z_{A}-z_{B}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{xy},r_{yz},r_{zx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{xy},r_{yz},r_{zx}</annotation></semantics></math> indicate relative positioning along each axis (e.g., front/back, left/right, above/below). It choose the axis with the greatest difference to label the dominant relation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">3) <span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">3D Video Grounding.</span> For frame <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in the camera coordinate system, the 3D bounding box of an object can be described with dimensions, center position, and optional rotations:</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{BBox}_{t}=(l_{t},w_{t},h_{t},x_{t},y_{t},z_{t},\mathrm{yaw}_{t},\mathrm{pitch}_{t},\mathrm{roll}_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>BBox</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>yaw</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>pitch</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>roll</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{BBox}_{t}=(l_{t},w_{t},h_{t},x_{t},y_{t},z_{t},\mathrm{yaw}_{t},\mathrm{pitch}_{t},\mathrm{roll}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l_{t},w_{t},h_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l_{t},w_{t},h_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> are the object dimensions, <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t},y_{t},z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the center position, and (yaw<sub id="A2.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">t</span></sub>, pitch<sub id="A2.SS2.p5.2.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">t</span></sub>, roll<sub id="A2.SS2.p5.2.3" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">t</span></sub> ) are optional rotation angles if available.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">4) <span id="A2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Pose Estimation.</span> Given the camera’s initial pose <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{0},o_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{0},o_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, the pose <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{t},o_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{t},o_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained using the extrinsic-derived matrices <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (rotation) and <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (translation):</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}=R_{t}p_{0}+T_{t},o_{t}=o_{0}+\Delta o_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}=R_{t}p_{0}+T_{t},o_{t}=o_{0}+\Delta o_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the position, <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orientation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">5) <span id="A2.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Displacement and Path Length.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=(x_{i},y_{i},z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=(x_{i},y_{i},z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> be the position at time <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The displacement <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0n}</annotation></semantics></math> and path length <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{traj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>traj</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{traj}}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed as:</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0n}=\sqrt{(x_{n}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{n}-y_{0})^{2}+(z_{n}-z_{0})^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0n}=\sqrt{(x_{n}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{n}-y_{0})^{2}+(z_{n}-z_{0})^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{traj}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sqrt{(x_{i}-x_{i-1})^{2}+(y_{i}-y_{i-1})^{2}+(z_{i}-z_{i-1})^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>traj</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{traj}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sqrt{(x_{i}-x_{i-1})^{2}+(y_{i}-y_{i-1})^{2}+(z_{i}-z_{i-1})^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the straight-line distance from the initial to the final position; <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{traj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>traj</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{traj}}</annotation></semantics></math> sums consecutive segment lengths for the entire path.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">6) <span id="A2.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Speed and Acceleration.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> be the time interval between consecutive frames. Then the speed <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and acceleration <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are:</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=\frac{d_{i}}{\Delta t},a_{i}=\frac{v_{i}-v_{i-1}}{\Delta t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=\frac{d_{i}}{\Delta t},a_{i}=\frac{v_{i}-v_{i-1}}{\Delta t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the displacement between adjacent frames, <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the speed at time <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the acceleration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">7) <span id="A2.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Ego-Centric Orientation.</span> If <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the camera orientation (azimuth) at time <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, then the orientation change <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{t}=\theta_{t}-\theta_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{t}=\theta_{t}-\theta_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p">This indicates how much the camera has rotated relative to its initial azimuth.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">8) <span id="A2.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Trajectory Description.</span> It applies the Ramer-DouglasPeucker (RDP) algorithm to simplify the sequence of positions into key line segments. The resulting polyline is described in a piecewise manner (<span id="A2.SS2.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, “go straight for 30m, turn left 85°, then go straight for 20m, …”), providing a concise representation of complex motion trajectories.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Implementation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span> focus on the pre-processing stage of <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MLLMs</span>, which samples one frame for every four frames from the given spatial video. For fair evaluation, we adopt 8 frames as input to test each <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MLLMs</span> for the given videos. For obtaining visual diversity and balancing efficiency, we utilize <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">YOLOv8</span>-Tiny, named <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">YOLOv8n</span> from Ultralytics<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics</a></span></span></span> for faster detection. All experiments are conducted on NVIDIA 8<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>A6000 and 6<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>A800. In actual development, to accelerate the overall testing process, we first utilize Motion construction and YOLO to process each sampled frame from videos for subsequent evaluation calls, which stores the corresponding spatial information. In evaluation, we call the stored spatial information from the last step and perform the <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Balanced-TopK</span> sampling and <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Spatiotemporal Encoding</span> techniques in each question and answer process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we utilize <span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VSI-Bench</span> for evaluation and leverage <span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">InternVL3-8B</span> as the baseline model. We investigate the effect of each technique proposed in our <span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">See&amp;Trek</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Ablation studies of each component of <span id="A2.T7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Balanced-Top<math id="A2.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</figcaption>
